; XInputProxy.def - export definition
; IMPORTANT: ordinals MUST match the real xinput1_3.dll exactly.
; Some games import XINPUT1_3.dll by ORDINAL (2,3,5), not by name (via a
; custom XInput wrapper DLL). If ordinals are off, the wrapper calls the wrong functions (e.g. calling
; GetAudioDeviceIds when it expects GetState) and controller input breaks.
; Real xinput1_3.dll ordinals (Wine .spec == MS binary):
;   1=DllMain 2=GetState 3=SetState 4=GetCapabilities 5=Enable
;   6=GetDSoundAudioDeviceGuids 7=GetBatteryInformation 8=GetKeystroke 100=GetStateEx
; GetAudioDeviceIds was added in xinput1_4 (absent in 1.3); the game's main exe
; resolves it by name via GetProcAddress, so export it named at @9.
EXPORTS
    XInputGetState @2
    XInputSetState @3
    XInputGetCapabilities @4
    XInputEnable @5
    XInputGetDSoundAudioDeviceGuids @6
    XInputGetBatteryInformation @7
    XInputGetKeystroke @8
    XInputGetAudioDeviceIds @9